      formula: String.raw`F \cong \operatorname{Hom}(-, X) \cong \operatorname{Hom}(-, X') \;\Rightarrow\; X \cong X'`,
      text: "If a presheaf F is represented by X with universal element u and by X′ with universal element u′, then there is exactly one isomorphism X → X′ that carries u′ to u. Every object defined by a universal property is unique up to unique isomorphism.",
      proof: "An isomorphism Hom(−, X) ≅ F ≅ Hom(−, X′) of presheaves comes, because the Yoneda embedding is fully faithful, from exactly one isomorphism X → X′; under the Yoneda lemma it carries u′ to u.",
