      text: "For every monad T on C the forgetful functor from T-algebras to C creates all limits that exist in C: the limit of the underlying objects carries a unique algebra structure making it the limit of the algebras.",
      proof: "The structure maps of the algebras form a cone from T(lim) to the diagram; its factorisation through the limit is the required structure map, and the algebra laws follow from uniqueness of factorisations.",
